::MCR_U06_L01_GuidedPractice_Q01::
Question ID: MCR_U06_L01_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: Support-only embedded MLA.MCR.MC standards - No primary Unit 6 GM standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Which unit would most likely be used to measure the length of a classroom?
{
~A. gallons#Gallons measure volume, not length. Match the unit to what is being measured before calculating.
=B. feet#Correct. Feet measure length and are reasonable for the size of a classroom.
~C. pounds#Pounds measure weight, not length. The lesson focus is choosing a unit that matches the dimension.
~D. minutes#Minutes measure time, not length. Use a length unit for classroom length.
}
::MCR_U06_L01_GuidedPractice_Q02::
Question ID: MCR_U06_L01_GP_Q02
MLA Standard: Support-only embedded MLA.MCR.MC standards - No primary Unit 6 GM standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Convert 4 feet to inches.
{
~A. 16 inches#This uses an incorrect conversion factor. One foot has 12 inches, so multiply by 12.
~B. 48 feet#This gives the correct number but keeps the original unit. The converted unit must be inches.
~C. 4 inches#This does not convert the measurement. A conversion changes the number while keeping the same real-world length.
=D. 48 inches#Correct. Since 1 foot = 12 inches, 4 x 12 = 48 inches.
}
::MCR_U06_L01_GuidedPractice_Q03::
Question ID: MCR_U06_L01_GP_Q03
MLA Standard: Support-only embedded MLA.MCR.MC standards - No primary Unit 6 GM standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Convert 120 minutes to hours.
{
=A. 2 hours#Correct. Since 60 minutes = 1 hour, 120 divided by 60 = 2 hours.
~B. 60 hours#This confuses the conversion fact with the answer. Divide minutes by 60 to convert to hours.
~C. 180 hours#This adds 60 instead of converting. Use the equal measurement 60 minutes = 1 hour.
~D. 7200 hours#This multiplies by 60, which makes the number far too large when changing minutes to hours.
}
::MCR_U06_L01_GuidedPractice_Q04::
Question ID: MCR_U06_L01_GP_Q04
MLA Standard: Support-only embedded MLA.MCR.MC standards - No primary Unit 6 GM standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Which measurement describes area?
{
~A. 8 feet#Feet describe length. Area uses square units.
~B. 3 gallons#Gallons describe volume. Area measures flat space.
=C. 20 square inches#Correct. Square inches describe area because the unit is squared.
~D. 12 minutes#Minutes describe time. The dimension must match the measurement type.
}
::MCR_U06_L01_GuidedPractice_Q05::
Question ID: MCR_U06_L01_GP_Q05
MLA Standard: Support-only embedded MLA.MCR.MC standards - No primary Unit 6 GM standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
A shelf is 2 yards long. How many feet long is the shelf?
{
~A. 2 feet#This does not convert yards to feet. One yard is longer than one foot.
=B. 6 feet#Correct. Since 1 yard = 3 feet, 2 x 3 = 6 feet.
~C. 12 feet#This uses the inches-per-foot conversion instead of yards to feet. Use 1 yard = 3 feet.
~D. 24 feet#This combines unrelated conversions. Convert yards to feet with 3 feet per yard.
}
